WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.475
Why check on the device?

2
00:00:01.475 --> 00:00:05.975
Because a value is only right or wrong
against the stage its ring is at.

3
00:00:05.975 --> 00:00:10.999
Network protection reading two, audit, is
exactly right on a ring still auditing,

4
00:00:10.999 --> 00:00:13.663
and drift on a ring that
should be blocking.

5
00:00:13.663 --> 00:00:16.550
By the end of this chapter
you can say, ring by ring,

6
00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:20.304
whether devices enforce the
prevention settings at the stage

7
00:00:20.304 --> 00:00:23.625
the change record set, and list
every device that doesn't.

8
00:00:23.625 --> 00:00:27.334
It's for the developers, the
platform owner who owns this gate,

9
00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:31.637
and the security operations center,
which reads the events every week.

10
00:00:31.637 --> 00:00:35.435
The setting values themselves live
in the Devices book's policies;

11
00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:36.980
this chapter checks them.
